This is the Game-o'-Life.  It should compile on almostanything with a curses library (BSD, SYSV, XENIX etc).The design is based on watching a running program andtrying to figure out the algorithm.  Cycles of 16 orless are found and noted, this value can be increased inthe source.A couple of example files are included: style, line, symand death.  If you come up with a good file then pleasemail it so I can have a look.Usage: life [file]This game is probably too dinky for comp.sources.games.Stacey Campbelluunet!sco!staceyc